Example 1 – common numerical factor
  Simplify &frac{6x}{9}
  HCF of 6 and 9 is 3
  Divide both by 3
  &frac{6x}{9} = &frac{2x}{3}
  &frac{2x}{3}
  (Divide numerator and denominator by their HCF.)

Example 2 – common variable factor
  Simplify &frac{x² + 3x}{x}
  Factorise numerator: x(x + 3)
  Rewrite: &frac{x(x + 3)}{x}
  Cancel x: = x + 3
  = x + 3
  (Factorise the numerator to reveal the common factor.)

Simplify each algebraic fraction fully.

(a) &frac{5x + 10}{x + 2}
(b) &frac{x² − 9}{x² + 6x + 9}
(c) &frac{2x² − 8}{2x + 4}
(d) &frac{x² + x − 12}{x² − 16}
(e) &frac{x² − 6x + 9}{x² − 9}
